From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepBlend_Walking::Perform reports not
 done for a non-finite range instead of walking it

BRepBlend_Walking::Perform takes the walk's start parameter, its end parameter and the flecheur
Fleche, and every caller (ChFi3d_Builder::ComputeData and its siblings) tests IsDone() afterwards.
Nothing checked that the three are finite.

On the model attached to OCCT#1576 (FreeCAD#21369), BRepFilletAPI_MakeChamfer at distance 1 on any
of 12 of its 36 edges calls it with Pmax = -inf and Fleche = inf. The origin is the extension that
ChFi3d_ChBuilder's ExtentSpineOnCommonFace gives two chamfer spines meeting at a vertex: for spine
tangents that are parallel (cosalpha = 1, sinalpha = 0) it computes tga = sinalpha / temp = 0 and
d = dis / tga = +infinity, then calls Spine->SetFirstParameter(-inf). The ElSpine range
(-inf, +inf) becomes wf and wl in ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine, and from them Pmax
and Fleche = (wl - wf) * fleche.

Inside the walk, CorrectExtremityOnOneRst builds Extrema_ExtPC(PntOnEnd, ElSpine) over that range
with a NaN point, and Extrema_GGExtPC::Perform reads out of range: a SIGSEGV that no catch (...)
in a bridge can reach, since OCC_CATCH_SIGNALS is inert in this build. Upstream IR declines the
same 12 edges (IsDone() == false).

The change returns from Perform with done = false when the start parameter, the end parameter or
Fleche is not finite. That is the state every caller already handles for a walk that failed, and
a finite range reaches exactly the code it reached before. The infinite extension itself is left
alone: skipping it was tried and turns 12 formerly declined edges of the same model into done
chamfers that BRepCheck rejects, which is worse than declining them.

Found by instrumenting the pinned kernel with override-linked copies of BRepBlend_Walking.cxx,
ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx and ChFi3d_ChBuilder.cxx (Scripts/repro/3350-chamfer-extrema-sigsegv/): the
first print is "cos=1 sin=0 dis1=1 dis2=1 d1plus=inf d2plus=inf" and everything downstream
(Pmax=-inf, Fleche=inf, hguide first=-inf last=inf) follows from it. On the OCCT#1576 model,
chamfer d = 1 on each of the 36 edges one at a time: 12 SIGSEGV before, 0 after; the 12 report
IsDone() == false.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3350.

--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #include <NCollection_Array2.hxx>
 #include <gce_MakePln.hxx>
 #include <gp_Pnt2d.hxx>
+#include <cmath>
 #include <math_FunctionSetRoot.hxx>
 #include <math_Gauss.hxx>

@@ -196,6 +197,12 @@
     line->Clear();
     doextremities = false;
   }
+  // A walk over a non-finite range is undefined: CorrectExtremityOnOneRst would project a NaN
+  // point onto a guide of infinite parameter range. Report not done, as for any failed walk.
+  if (!std::isfinite(Pdep) || !std::isfinite(Pmax) || !std::isfinite(Fleche))
+  {
+    return;
+  }
   tolpoint3d = Tol3d;
   tolgui     = std::abs(TolGuide);
   fleche     = std::abs(Fleche);
